# COMPARE - Compare two files byte by byte

```text
COMPARE file1 file2 [options]
```

## Find differences

The default report lists up to 20 differences. /SUM gives totals,
/COUNT=n sets a display limit, and /SIDE shows paired bytes. Both inputs
remain available for inspection.

```text
C0:COMPARE D0:OLD.COM D0:NEW.COM /SIDE
```

## Compare a range

/FROM and /FROM2 specify starting offsets in the first and second file.
/LEN limits the comparison. These three values are hexadecimal byte
counts or offsets.

```text
C0:COMPARE D0:OLD.COM D0:NEW.COM /FROM=100 /FROM2=100 /LEN=20
```
